==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Himeyuri Ninetails''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Fox Queen Himeyuri''' at level 30 using [[Catfruit]] and XP.

==Strategy/Usage==
Himeyuri has access to a top "Research" effect UP [[Cat Combo|Combo]] [[Kimono Champs (Combo)|Kimono Champs]], which is one of only three Research Up L combos in the game. She is also extremely useful against Floating and Angel enemies due to the fact that she has a near-guaranteed chance to slow them for a long time. She excels at keeping [[Teacher Bun Bun]], and other Floating Enemies ranging below 400 at bay, however as with the rest of the set, beware her multihit. This is because her multihit may sometimes interrupt high-KB enemies and fail to proc and CC them, with relevant examples including [[Angelic Gory]] and [[Li'l Bun Bun]]; this may cause Himeyuri to fall off until you get her Talents, where she sees new light in Uncanny Legends. Unfortunately, her main Angel niche is replaced by [[Bishop Cat (Rare Cat)|Sanzo Cat]] as he has an identical set of abilities and is stackable. This limits Himeyuri's non-relic usage to a few things:
*Kimono Champs in {{4c}} stages
*As a failsafe in case Sanzo doesn't proc
*As a backup DPS unit, as she has serviceable DPS for a range of 445
*As an Uber CC unit if Sanzo is outranged in the cases of [[Winged Pigge]] and [[Angelic Sleipnir]] and their own relevant stages. Overall, her usage is not to be denied as situationally useful albeit replaced after unlocking the Talented powercreep.

==='''Talents'''===
'''Target Relic''' and '''Curse Immune''' allow Fox Queen Himeyuri to control [[:Category:Relic Enemies|Relics]] while attacking them. Those talents cost lots of NP, but they are worth it due to the lack of non-Uber crowd-controllers who work against Relic enemies. Her range of 445 gives her usage against many tough targets, including [[Primeval Cyclone]], [[M. Ost]], and even [[Relic Bun-Bun]]. However, if you own [[Master Uril (Special Cat)|Master Uril]], this talent can safely be ignored due to his more consistent Slow and Surge, not to mention not requiring any NP. Even if Himeyuri does have higher range, most suitable Relics that can be slowed such as [[M. Ost]], swarms of [[Sir Rel|Sir Rels]] and [[Oldhorn]] are outranged by Uril safely, not to mention that ones that haven't been slowed yet will simply run into the Surges he creates.

As she has strong stats for her range, '''Attack Buff''' and '''HP Buff''' can be considered, though Attack Buff takes priority here. This is after [[Catseye]]s have already been used.

Finally, she has '''Resist Freeze''', which is only situational. It can be used against [[Henry]] and perhaps even [[Golem Sunfish]], though they would still not really be worth the NP cost.

==='''Ultra Talents'''===
'''Mini-Surge''' is Himeyuri's most notable ultra talent. It's capable of raising her uptime and her dps, while also adding some piercing into the mix. This can alleviate some issues regarding her weaker matchups, as now she can strike through and control even more of the field, which is good against any enemy that can outrange her.

Unfortunately, the positives end very quickly. The mini-surge is generally inconsistent in just a few too many ways for it to be a good investment. From it being only a 50%, to it's incredibly wide spawn range, Himeyuri may not struggle to create a surge, since she creates them as often as she slows, but she only gets a 57% chance for a surge to also carry her slow, and having the surge hit the enemies makes things even more complicated. Offense is also a pretty rough situation as it only gives her 10% more offense, which is still inconsistent. This is already a poor buff, but the high investment needed makes things even worse.

Himeyuri's only other ultra talent is '''Cost Down''', which decreases her cost by 750. This is fine in theory, but hard to recommend simply because it's very expensive to get to, especially for an Uber with a cost that isn't too high.

Himeyuri's ultra talents are recommendable under the very small circumstances in which you need a crowd controlling sniper for floating enemies or angels and are willing to pay any price for it because of some difficult stages. However, if you already have one, you can completely ignore these very minimal improvements.

